#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "911977f9-4dd7-5952-a7d2-5e7840939b58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286104} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb95726-da34-5373-afcd-2fe81b267f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286105} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d4bc3d-a55e-5bbb-8cf3-be60cc08dce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286106} {:answer/id #uuid "7a7d6c0b-89d4-58f6-b838-87a105cabcb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286107} {:answer/id #uuid "1595331b-914e-55d1-ad79-8a6281f2e79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "911977f9-4dd7-5952-a7d2-5e7840939b58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286104} :answer-field/id #uuid "7765a4c1-9acf-5c4a-b959-40fe56dae2b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "18446b37-20cc-5e44-a427-24676c932277" :question/math-academy-id "q-12124" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(-2,-1),(1,3),(2,-3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(-3,1)$\n- $(-3,2)$\n- $(1,-2)$" :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${90}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(1,-2),(-3,1),(3,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
